// V8 Coverage Instrumentation Overview
// ====================================
// V8 implements code coverage instrumentation through multiple mechanisms:
// 1. JavaScript function coverage (invocation counts)
// 2. Block/edge coverage for JavaScript (basic block execution)
// 3. WebAssembly basic block coverage
// 4. Basic block profiling for compiler optimization

// Coverage Modes:
// --------------
// debug::CoverageMode::kBestEffort       - Function-level, no instrumentation
// debug::CoverageMode::kPreciseCount     - Function-level with precise counts
// debug::CoverageMode::kPreciseBinary    - Function-level binary (0/1)
// debug::CoverageMode::kBlockCount       - Block-level with counts
// debug::CoverageMode::kBlockBinary      - Block-level binary (0/1)

// Key Data Structures:
// -------------------
// CoverageInfo: Stores block coverage data attached to DebugInfo
//   - slot_count: number of coverage slots
//   - slots[slot_count]: CoverageInfoSlot array
// CoverageInfoSlot: {start_source_position, end_source_position, block_count}
// DebugInfo: Contains coverage_info field pointing to CoverageInfo
// SharedFunctionInfo: Has DebugInfo for coverage instrumentation
// FeedbackVector: Stores function invocation counts
